repository-code: "https://github.com/Apsiape/finite-contact-theory-public"
abstract: "A public release of Finite Contact Theory, a long-range finite reconstruction program. This v0.4 chapter publishes the inquiry calculus at finite-model scope: questions act as residual operators whose algebra is noncommutative in general and commutes exactly on order-blind (count-only) epistemic objects; the expected cost of any binary question protocol decomposes exactly as entropy plus belief mismatch plus slack (EC = H + KL + O, a second law of asking, refining the v0.3 selector debt); adaptive questioning strictly beats fixed questioning under a constrained question repertoire; and self-reference is lawful under grading while paradox is exactly type collapse. All results are machine-checked by a shipped dependency-free script; earlier chapters are unchanged and every unearned generalization is held open by name."
version: "0.4.0"
date-released: "2026-07-13"
